    "done_when": "tests/test_control_gate_checks_facts.py holds four cases:\n- test_a_control_whose_run_exits_zero_is_refused\n- a control whose added-failure set against the baseline is empty is refused\n- a control that exits non-zero with at least one added failure is admitted even when its declaration shares no words with the log\n- a control whose wording matches but whose run exited zero is refused\n\nThe cases the substring test decides differently fail at the base revision, with that arm logged, and pass at the head.\n\nThe declared mutation is applied in a scratch copy and the file observed to fail, with the mutation verbatim on the red log's first line.\n\nThe gate `/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q tests/test_control_gate_checks_facts.py` exits 0 from the worktree. The existing test files that exercise `_require_declared_negative_control` show no added failures by id against the base.",
    "estimated_hours": 5.0,
    "goal": "Plan crew-runtime-positive-controls §20: the negative-control gate checks facts, not words. Today `_require_declared_negative_control` in reckon/crew/promotion.py (defined near :4070, called near :4455) admits a control by a verbatim substring test (`if declaration not in text:` near :4152). That admits a log whose first line repeats the declaration while its run exited zero. It also cannot see a control whose failure set equals the baseline's.\n\nReplace that substring comparison with a fact check. A control is admitted when its run exits non-zero and fails at least one test that the baseline does not fail, whatever its wording. It is refused when it exits zero, and refused when its added-failure set against the baseline is empty.\n\nThe `none: <reason>` escape, the gate-passing exemption and the --waive-negative-control escape stay as they are.",
